olls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "South Carolina's partisan lean sits about eight points to the right of the nation, making it a reliably Republican state in presidential contests. The 2028 race is open, with the incumbent president term-limited, and neither party has a settled nominee, published polling, or fundraising figures in the state.\n\nWith no polls or expert ratings available, the forecast rests on the state's partisan fundamentals. That lean makes the Republican side the favorite, while a wide uncertainty band reflects the open field and the absence of candidate-specific evidence. South Carolina's selection to lead the Democratic primary calendar has drawn national attention to the nominating contest, but that shapes the primary rather than the general election. The race is rated Lean Republican, with room to move once nominees emerge and polling begins.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1807, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2319, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2236, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2334, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.2281, "margin": -8.0}]}